WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.770
If you frequent the internet

00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:07.649
you have likely seen memes in videos with a character known as Doomer and or any of his counter characters boomer bloomer and

00:00:07.809 --> 00:00:14.609
Zoomer if you have not these are them each of these characters represents a distinct personality type usually associated with a specific

00:00:14.889 --> 00:00:20.458
Generation within current society. The Doomer character is especially popular and is what we will be focusing on here

00:00:20.710 --> 00:00:23.790
The Doomer is an individual who was typically in their 20s and male

00:00:23.859 --> 00:00:26.939
Although a Doomer in the philosophical sense does not need to be either

00:00:27.099 --> 00:00:30.539
he or she does however need to be someone who feels a sense of aimlessness and

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:32.439
loneliness and is consequently

00:00:32.439 --> 00:00:34.090
stricken with a deep despair for life

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:35.790
For the numeron life is meaningless

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:40.559
And the world is inevitably doomed by humanity's ignorance greed and futility as a result

00:00:40.559 --> 00:00:47.069
The do mercy is little to no reason in engaging in traditional pursuits and thus retreats from society into apathetic isolation

00:00:47.110 --> 00:00:50.700
This character is often used in videos and memes to illustrate various

00:00:50.949 --> 00:00:54.899
Experiences that come with this pessimistic sense of life things like working a dead-end job

00:00:55.300 --> 00:01:02.129
Struggling to maintain or get over romantic relationships excessive drinking and smoking feeling alienated from one's friends and family, etc

00:01:02.770 --> 00:01:08.309
This characters popularity and widespread relatability is very telling about the conditions of the modern person

00:01:08.619 --> 00:01:13.649
specifically that of the current young adult generation it reveals the depth of pessimism and nihilism being

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:16.349
experienced a hopelessness for both the now and for the future

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:24.360
one of the dimmers counter characters is the boomer the name being derived from the term baby boomer an individual born between 1946 and

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:30.869
1964 two generations or so before the Doomer however, the age and generation of a boomer does not necessarily matter

00:01:30.869 --> 00:01:33.869
What does matter is this characters contrasting outlook on life?

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:36.269
opposed to the Doomer the boomer possesses a

00:01:36.369 --> 00:01:41.909
Positive can-do attitude more specifically in the context of the meme the boomers attitude exists in a naive

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:47.549
Blissful ignorance of truth the boomer chugs along and they're ignorant delusion unaware of the reality in which they live

00:01:47.890 --> 00:01:53.849
Mistakenly thinking they have it all under control where the Doomer is aware of the world's conditions and consequently pessimistic about them

00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:58.710
The boomer is unaware and thus ignorantly blissful unlike the baby boomers

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:02.399
The Doomer was born in or around the 90s and grew up through an era when technology

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:06.119
Developed at an unprecedented rate in an exceptionally small amount of time

00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:12.599
The advent of the Internet as well as affordable Internet devices would completely change the way people could experience and understand the world

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:18.269
During this internet generation children and young adults had access to a completely open and constant flow of information

00:02:18.519 --> 00:02:23.849
An ability to see/hear talk with an engage in the entire world in real-time all the time

00:02:24.129 --> 00:02:27.959
The world would shrink down to fit in the palm of one's hand allowing one to easily

00:02:27.959 --> 00:02:30.149
See just how absurd chaotic and meaningless

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:31.659
it truly is as

00:02:31.659 --> 00:02:38.369
A result a huge portion of an entire generation would realize early on that things weren't all good that the can do positive

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:42.359
Attitude of the boomer was outdated and ignorant of what was really going on

00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:50.549
with lingering counterculture narratives from the 60s and 70s a decreasing popularity and Christianity following the Second World War and an

00:02:50.709 --> 00:02:52.269
increasing access to information

00:02:52.269 --> 00:02:54.479
This generation would be left with no traditional

00:02:54.639 --> 00:02:59.699
Meaning or hope to fall back on the generation where many find a piece of themselves in the Doomer

00:03:01.060 --> 00:03:06.569
So now what are we doomed to exist in a world where the options are either blissful ignorance or informed?

00:03:06.579 --> 00:03:11.369
Melancholy in order to better understand and deal with growing pessimistic and nihilistic tendencies

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:16.649
It is helpful to refer to the work of 19th century philosophers Arthur Schopenhauer and Friedrich Nietzsche

00:03:17.349 --> 00:03:20.668
Arthur Schopenhauer is often regarded as the philosopher of pessimism

00:03:20.949 --> 00:03:26.879
Arguably the original Doomer like the dimmers outlook for Schopenhauer life is in fact riddled with unavoidable pain

00:03:27.159 --> 00:03:31.589
Meaninglessness and absurdity for Schopenhauer we are prisoners to our unconscious instinct to survive

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:38.489
Reproduce in sustain existence and in the traditional sense everything we do in life is merely a product of this irrational force

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:42.780
Void of any purpose other than to continue to sustain itself as a result

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:44.169
We live a life of delusion

00:03:44.169 --> 00:03:50.339
Constantly in a frenzy trying to impress sexual partners in order to reproduce and trying to accomplish things in order to find happiness

00:03:50.709 --> 00:03:57.328
Schopenhauer writes there's only one inborn error and that is the notion that we exist in order to be happy so long as we persist

00:03:57.329 --> 00:04:00.089
In this inborn error the world seems to us full of contradictions

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:06.090
for at every step and things great and small we are bound to experience that the world in life are certainly not arranged for the

00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:08.310
purpose of maintaining a happy existence in

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:14.879
Schopenhauer's mind we want so badly to believe that we exist to be happy and to have specific purpose but with an honest

00:04:15.069 --> 00:04:19.649
Examination we realize we do not this perspective does not fall far from that of the Doomer

00:04:20.019 --> 00:04:26.218
Arguably neither the Doomer nor Schopenhauer are necessarily wrong in their assessments of life life is in fact linked with K

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:33.099
Ah, Spain and fundamental meaninglessness the real problem. However is not found in this realization, but how this realization is handled

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:37.629
Schopenhauer offered two solutions for the realization of life's meaningless suffering

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:40.040
asceticism and art

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:47.860
Asceticism is the disciplined avoidance of pleasure an overcoming of the unconscious desire and pursuit for the selfish immaterial be it things like sex

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:50.020
Vanity money social status, etc

00:04:50.510 --> 00:04:56.260
Schopenhauer felt that by obtaining control over the ceaseless yearning for things one can find a form of happiness in the present moment

00:04:56.720 --> 00:04:57.320
however

00:04:57.320 --> 00:05:00.249
Schopenhauer also acknowledged the sheer difficulty in accomplishing this feat

00:05:00.590 --> 00:05:07.119
for it is not enough to merely realize the senselessness of one's behaviors in order to stop them from occurring the level of discipline and

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:11.200
Commitment required would prove immensely difficult for even the wisest of individuals

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:19.120
Alternatively in Schopenhauer provided one other solution engaging in the aesthetics of art and philosophy as much as possible in this Schopenhauer

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:24.429
Suggested that things like poetry theater music paintings literature theory, etc

00:05:24.430 --> 00:05:30.760
Have the power to reveal and share truth a truth that liberates the individual during the moments he or she is engaging in it

00:05:30.980 --> 00:05:34.839
By expressing our pains and sufferings or engaging in the expressions of others

00:05:34.840 --> 00:05:42.040
we feel less imprisoned and less disillusioned in ourself with this one does not need to find anything worthwhile or ultimately meaningful in the

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:49.779
Materialistic or traditional world beyond the mere expression of one's disinterest and pain within it in expressing pain and absurdity through arts and philosophy

00:05:50.090 --> 00:05:54.910
The pain and absurdity is transmuted into wonder and purpose for oneself as well as others

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:58.420
Interestingly enough the Doomer meme itself embodies this idea

00:05:58.420 --> 00:06:04.599
the creation sharing an engaging of Doomer content is an example of a Doomer expressing their sense of Doom and

00:06:04.820 --> 00:06:09.369
Translating it into something enjoyable and meaningful in an attempt to take this idea further

00:06:09.370 --> 00:06:14.020
We will look to the philosophy of Friedrich Nietzsche a philosopher renowned for his nihilistic take on life

00:06:14.270 --> 00:06:17.589
nihilism is the belief in nothing the principle that nothing has any

00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:22.690
Fundamental meaning at the end of itself and that life is and will always involve a suffering through this meaninglessness

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:25.240
During his life in the 19th century

00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:32.080
Nietzsche found that traditional religion ceased to help the modern person in dealing with the pains of life and that nihilism was the only rational

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:33.890
And practical approach that remained

00:06:33.890 --> 00:06:39.699
However for Nietzsche the meaninglessness found in Nile is did not suggest that we should give up and retreat into a dull

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:47.710
Apathetic life rather the realization that life is meaningless permits the individual to look inside him or herself and create their own meaning and self-identity

00:06:47.990 --> 00:06:51.280
The world is full of systems and pressures to conform to the collective

00:06:51.650 --> 00:06:55.389
Religions traditions and mass movements that attempt to lead us in certain arbitrary directions

00:06:55.730 --> 00:07:00.549
The individual Nietzsche writes has always had to struggle to keep from being overwhelmed by the tribe

00:07:00.550 --> 00:07:01.510
If you try it

00:07:01.510 --> 00:07:07.450
You will be lonely often and sometimes frightened but no price is too high to pay for the privilege of owning yourself

00:07:07.580 --> 00:07:09.290
the pressure of accepting mass

00:07:09.290 --> 00:07:15.010
Methodologies and principles in life is has and will always be immense the resistance of such comes with feelings of alienation

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:21.999
And hardship however for Nietzsche the pain of caving in is infinitely worse in the context of modern times

00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:28.570
Perhaps the Doomer feels a heightened alienation from the world because the internet compounds the weight of social pressure and a sense of detachment

00:07:29.030 --> 00:07:29.530
however

00:07:29.530 --> 00:07:36.070
This experience of alienation and despair is not unnatural nor without value rather one must walk deliberately through the mud of life

00:07:36.380 --> 00:07:39.070
realizing that there will be ongoing pains and challenges in their

00:07:39.380 --> 00:07:44.350
Self-actualization and instead of turning away from them lean into them and face the sufferings head-on

00:07:44.660 --> 00:07:48.880
Developing themselves and their personal meaning no matter how uncommon or hard it may be

00:07:49.490 --> 00:07:52.630
Nietzsche felt that the key to suffering is knowing how to use suffering I

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:59.260
Assessed the power of a will by how much resistance pain torture it endures and knows how to turn to its advantage Nietzsche rides

00:07:59.930 --> 00:08:04.959
By inviting suffering in and recognizing it as an opportunity to develop wisdom and resilience

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:11.139
We utilize it as a method of creating our own purpose and greatness in the fundamental pain and meaninglessness of life

00:08:11.139 --> 00:08:13.989
We must not find ourselves with an indifference that renders us

00:08:14.150 --> 00:08:21.310
Lethargic and paralysed away from caring about anything but rather an indifference that inspires us to create meaning and care for things we deem enjoyable

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:22.370
and engaging

00:08:22.370 --> 00:08:23.810
for both Nietzsche and Schopenhauer

00:08:23.810 --> 00:08:26.229
The greatest reason for life is found in the self

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:33.880
Realization and self expression of one's unique truth the utilization of the suffering and chaos in life and turning it into wonder wisdom and greatness

00:08:34.159 --> 00:08:36.879
With this in mind if we square away our life as best

00:08:36.880 --> 00:08:42.489
We can accepting the inevitable chaos and suffering if we obtain the money we can want to need to sustain our life

00:08:42.589 --> 00:08:48.789
attempting to keep a close eye on our unconscious irrational desires and if we live with an interest to create personal meaning in

00:08:49.060 --> 00:08:55.479
And expressive activities then we can build a life worth living even in the face of apparent chaos doom or futility

00:08:55.850 --> 00:08:59.290
this attitude can be found in the hopeful Doomer character bloomer a

00:08:59.570 --> 00:09:03.700
Character who in the meme possesses the awareness of the sad and painful realities of life

00:09:03.700 --> 00:09:09.369
but still sees that there could be purpose to it all still sees that there's an opportunity for meaning and wonder to be created and

00:09:09.529 --> 00:09:14.559
experienced and that however messy the world may be it is still worth playing in and trying to make the most of

00:09:34.360 --> 00:09:36.360
You

